user_prompt:
Variables are listed below in random order. Use the exact id strings.
[
  {
    "id": "pollution"
  },
  {
    "id": "smoker"
  },
  {
    "id": "cancer"
  },
  {
    "id": "dyspnoea"
  },
  {
    "id": "xray"
  }
]

Task: propose a causal order prior. Earlier variables are potential causes or upstream conditions; later variables are downstream effects, measurements, symptoms, decisions, or aggregate outcomes.

Return one JSON object with this schema:
{
  "ordered_nodes": ["exact id 1", "exact id 2", "..."],
  "confidence": 0.0,
  "high_confidence_pairs": [
    {"before": "exact id", "after": "exact id", "confidence": 0.0}
  ],
  "rationale": "brief, no more than 80 words"
}

Constraints: ordered_nodes must contain every provided id exactly once; do not invent nodes; if evidence is weak, still provide the best semantic prior and lower the confidence.

raw_response:
{
  "ordered_nodes": ["pollution", "smoker", "cancer", "xray", "dyspnoea"],
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "high_confidence_pairs": [
    {"before": "pollution", "after": "cancer", "confidence": 0.93},
    {"before": "smoker", "after": "cancer", "confidence": 0.95},
    {"before": "cancer", "after": "dyspnoea", "confidence": 0.9},
    {"before": "cancer", "after": "xray", "confidence": 0.88},
    {"before": "pollution", "after": "dyspnoea", "confidence": 0.72},
    {"before": "smoker", "after": "dyspnoea", "confidence": 0.7}
  ],
  "rationale": "Smoking and pollution are upstream risk factors, cancer is the disease outcome, and dyspnoea and xray are downstream symptom/measurement variables. Xray is placed after cancer as a diagnostic test or resulting observation, while dyspnoea is a symptom typically caused by cancer or related illness."
}
